   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REBUILD Vanuatu (Resilient Earthquake Building Assessment and Infrastructure Linkage Development)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On December 17, 2024, a powerful 7.3 magnitude earthquake struck near Port Vila, Vanuatu&#x2019;s capital. Within 24 hours, a second 5.5 magnitude quake followed, triggering landslides and devastating infrastructure. Over 80,000 people have been affected, with many losing their homes and essential services. This disaster comes as communities are still recovering from twin cyclones in 2023, compounding the nation&#x2019;s vulnerability.Vanuatu, home to over 300,000 people across 83 islands, faces frequent eart</narrative>
  </description>
